@startuml
!include theme.puml
title Tuition payment | Durable intent and atomic settlement
autonumber
participant "Student UI\nvia gateway" as UI
participant "Finance API" as API
participant "Finance worker" as W
participant "reconcile_intent\nshared function" as R
database finance_db as DB
participant "Provider adapter" as PSP
activate UI
UI -> API : POST invoices/{id}/payment-intents
activate API
API -> DB : Read tenant invoice
activate DB
DB --> API : Invoice record
deactivate DB
API -> API : Check ownership + pending invoice
group Commit before external I/O
  API -> DB : INSERT intent + unique reference\npartial unique active-intent constraint
  activate DB
  API -> DB : COMMIT
  DB --> API : Durable pending intent
  deactivate DB
end
API -> PSP : request_to_pay(reference, amount, mobile)
activate PSP
alt Request accepted
  PSP --> API : Accepted / no settlement assertion
else Exception or timeout
  PSP --> API : Exception / timeout
end
deactivate PSP
opt Provider request failed
  API -> API : Log failure; keep intent pending
end
API --> UI : 201 intent (pending)
deactivate API
deactivate UI
loop Worker tick every 3 seconds (independent of browser polling)
  activate W
  W -> DB : Platform session; list pending intent IDs
  activate DB
  DB --> W : Pending IDs
  deactivate DB
  loop Each pending ID in its own session
    W -> R : reconcile_intent(session, gateway, id)
    activate R
    group Shared reconciliation body
      R -> DB : SELECT intent FOR UPDATE
      activate DB
      DB --> R : Locked intent or no match
      deactivate DB
      alt Missing or terminal intent
        R -> R : Use None / stored status; no duplicate posting
      else Pending intent
        R -> PSP : get_status(reference, requested_at, mobile)
        activate PSP
        PSP --> R : PENDING / FAILED / SUCCESSFUL
        deactivate PSP
        alt Provider PENDING
          R -> R : Keep intent pending
        else Provider FAILED
          R -> DB : Set intent failed; COMMIT
          activate DB
          DB --> R : Failed state committed
          deactivate DB
        else Provider SUCCESSFUL
          R -> DB : SELECT invoice FOR UPDATE
          activate DB
          DB --> R : Locked invoice
          deactivate DB
          group One ACID commit
            R -> DB : Set intent succeeded; if invoice unpaid:\nmark paid + balanced ledger + unique receipt;\nCOMMIT all settlement changes
            activate DB
            DB --> R : Settlement committed
            deactivate DB
          end
        end
      end
    end
    R --> W : None / pending / failed / succeeded
    deactivate R
    W -> DB : Close per-intent session;\nroll back any remaining read transaction
    activate DB
    DB --> W : Remaining locks released
    deactivate DB
  end
  deactivate W
end
loop Browser polls every 1.5 seconds while pending
  activate UI
  UI -> API : GET payment-intents/{id}
  activate API
  API -> DB : Read tenant intent + invoice; check ownership
  activate DB
  DB --> API : Owned intent and invoice
  deactivate DB
  opt Intent is still pending
    API -> R : reconcile_intent(session, gateway, id)
    activate R
    ref over R,PSP : Shared reconciliation body above (same row locks / atomic settlement)
    R --> API : Current status; identity-mapped intent updated
    deactivate R
  end
  API --> UI : 200 current payment intent
  deactivate API
  deactivate UI
end
activate UI
UI -> API : GET owned invoice receipt
activate API
API -> DB : Tenant + owner scoped invoice/receipt lookup
activate DB
DB --> API : Issued receipt for settled invoice
deactivate DB
API -> API : Render receipt PDF
API --> UI : application/pdf
deactivate API
deactivate UI
note over API,PSP
Bars show request, helper and query execution; dashed arrows are returns.
Worker and browser loops may overlap; they use the same locking helper.
Database locks survive individual query bars until transaction/session end.
Balanced settlement = cash debit + revenue credit, same posting_id and equal totals.
An already-paid invoice does not receive a second posting or receipt.
Callback body is only a reference hint; provider status is authoritative.
Current gateway blocks unauthenticated callback ingress.
Poller queries status; it does not resubmit a lost MTN request.
Provider call is inside the reconciliation lock lifetime.
end note
@enduml
